    "result_text": "The full build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented postcode-preferred locality derivation.\n\n**`LocalityResolver.java`** \u2014 Added a new `resolve(String city, String postcode)` overload that:\n1. Looks up the region by postcode range first (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) via a new private `fromPostcode` helper.\n2. Falls back to the existing city-to-region table (`resolve(String city)`) only when the postcode is `null`, unparseable, or in no known range.\n\nThe original city-only `resolve(String city)` is retained unchanged, because `PostcodeValidator` must keep validating a postcode against the *city's* declared region (e.g. reject a VIC postcode on a Sydney owner) \u2014 using postcode-preferred resolution there would make validation vacuous.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Updated the `locality` mapping expression to pass the postcode: `LocalityResolver.resolve(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())`.\n\nThis returns the same region for known cities (e.g. Sydney + 2000 \u2192 NSW) but disambiguates by postcode (e.g. an unknown city + 3000 \u2192 VIC), as required.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreRegionFromPostcodeRange`, `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity`) and the full suite pass: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
