    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. POST /api/owners is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (v1 controller, `@RequestMapping(\"/api\")` + the `OwnersApi` interface). Here is everything applied, in order.\n\n## Before the method body (framework layer)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`: the caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the request is rejected before any logic runs.\n\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`OwnerFieldsDto`, validated by the generated API interface; failures \u2192 400):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$` (letters, up to two separators).\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (like firstName, optional trailing `.`).\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern (?s).*\\S.*` (must contain a non-whitespace char).\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern (?s).*\\S.*`.\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^\\+?[0-9 ()\\-]+$` (loose syntactic form).\n   - `email` \u2014 optional; when present `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern`, `@Email` (syntactically valid).\n   - `postcode` \u2014 optional; when present `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`, `@Size(4)`.\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 `@Valid` ISO date (must parse).\n\n## Inside `addOwner`, in execution order\n\n3. **Map DTO \u2192 entity** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)`.\n\n4. **`normalizeOwnerFields(owner)`** \u2014 canonicalization + field-level validation, in this order:\n   - **Address normalize**: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`); **blank after normalization \u2192 400** (`InvalidAddressException`). Stored in canonical form.\n   - **Telephone normalize + validate** to E.164: strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+`/country code or assume `+61` (dropping one leading `0`); must be 8\u201315 digits, and national-number length must match country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210); **otherwise \u2192 400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`).\n   - **Email** lower-cased (null left as-is).\n   - **Postcode validate** against the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any 4-digit); only when present; **out of range \u2192 400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`). Stored unchanged.\n   - **Registration date**: default to server's current date when null, then roll a Saturday/Sunday forward to the following Monday (business-day adjustment). This adjusted date is what all date-derived logic uses.\n\n5. **`rejectDisallowedOwnerCreation(owner)`** \u2014 pre-persistence policy rejections, in order:\n   - **Daily limit**: if \u2265 `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` (100) owners already carry this (adjusted) registration date \u2192 **429** (`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`).\n   - **City capacity**: if the city already has \u2265 `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` (50) owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409** (`CityCapacityExceededException`).\n\n6. **`applyHouseholdMembership(owner, sharesHousehold)`**:\n   - Look up existing owners in the same household (same normalized last name + address).\n   - **Side-effect**: if the request set `sharesHousehold=true` **and** matching members exist, assign the new owner a stable `householdId` (SHA-256-derived) and write that same `householdId` onto every existing member whose id differs \u2014 **persisting each updated member via `clinicService.saveOwner`**.\n   - Set `householdSize` (1 if no shared household; else matched members + 1).\n\n7. **`rejectWhenIdentityInUse(owner)`**: compute the identity key `telephone|email|householdId` and scan all owners; if any existing owner has the same key \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`). (This single check subsumes the former separate telephone/email/household duplicate checks; it runs *after* household resolution because the key includes `householdId`.)\n\n8. **`assignDerivedFields(owner)`** \u2014 create-time derived fields, in order:\n   - `namesakeCount` \u2014 count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n   - `customerCode` \u2014 `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN = existing owners in that city + 1.\n   - `membershipNumber` \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (last two digits of the registration year).\n   - `bulkSignupWarning` \u2014 `true` if more than `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (80) owners already carry this registration date.\n\n9. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.\n\n10. **Audit log** \u2014 an `AUDIT` logger line: `Owner created: id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026`.\n\n11. **Response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 Created**.\n\nNote: `sharesHousehold` is write-only (consumed in step 6, never persisted or returned), and `updateOwner` (PUT) does **not** run steps 4\u201310 \u2014 those side-effects are specific to create."
